"use strict";
window.LC_CHUNKS=window.LC_CHUNKS||{};window.LC_CHUNKS["university_electrical_engineering_core_en"]=window.LC_CHUNKS["university_electrical_engineering_core_en"]||{};window.LC_CHUNKS["university_electrical_engineering_core_en"][8]={"university_electrical_engineering_core_en:M8-L1":"<article class=\"lesson-standard\"><h1 id=\"L1\">M8-L1 – Requirements, Sources and the Project Question<\/h1>\n<p><strong>Course area:<\/strong> M8 – Bachelor: Engineering Practice and Bachelor’s Project<\/p>\n<p><strong>Level:<\/strong> Bachelor<\/p>\n<p><strong>Prerequisites:<\/strong> <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering-core&amp;module=M6&amp;lesson=L1&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">Measurement\nchains<\/a>, <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering-core&amp;module=M6&amp;lesson=L4&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">Feedback<\/a>\nand <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering-core&amp;module=M6&amp;lesson=L6&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">Temperature\ncontrol<\/a>.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Learning objective:<\/strong> Break a technical question down\ninto verifiable requirements and specify suitable evidence for each\nobjective.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S1\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>The project question<\/h2>\n<p>A temperature controller is intended to maintain a constant\ntemperature rise above ambient in a simulated test room. A temporary\nenvironmental influence lowers the temperature. The sensor reading has a\nsmall periodic deviation and temporarily fails. The project question is:\n<strong>Which of the requirements specified in advance does the modelled\ncontroller meet in these three test cases?<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>The test concerns the temperature rise\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>T<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><msub><mi>T<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x=T-T_\\mathrm{amb}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nin kelvin. At\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mn>20<\/mn><msup><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mo>∘<\/mo><\/msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T_\\mathrm{amb}=20\\,^\\circ\\mathrm C<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>4<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x=4\\,\\mathrm K<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\ncorresponds to an absolute temperature reading of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>24<\/mn><msup><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mo>∘<\/mo><\/msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">24\\,^\\circ\\mathrm C<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nThe reference remains at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>4<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">4\\,\\mathrm K<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nThe plant, measurement chain and control input are computational models.\nWhat matters in the project is whether a claim can be traced to a\nrequirement, a file and a verifiable result.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S2\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Specify requirements before calculating<\/h2>\n<p>The frequency, duration and magnitude of a disturbance affect what a\ntest can demonstrate. We therefore define three explicit scenarios:<\/p>\n<ul class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><strong>Baseline:<\/strong> Reference step at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>t<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t=0<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nidealised calibrated measurement, without an external disturbance.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><strong>Disturbance:<\/strong> From\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>t<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>240<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t=240\\,\\mathrm s<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nconstant modelled cooling acts, represented in the plant equation by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>−<\/mi><mn>1<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d=-1\\,\\mathrm K<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><strong>Measurement chain:<\/strong> The same cooling, periodic\nmeasurement deviation and a measurement gap over\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>250<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s<\/mi><mo>≤<\/mo><mi>t<\/mi><mo>&lt;<\/mo><mn>260<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">250\\,\\mathrm s\\le t&lt;260\\,\\mathrm s<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col class=\"lc-col-third\">\n<col class=\"lc-col-third\">\n<col class=\"lc-col-third\">\n<\/colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>ID<\/th>\n<th>Test object<\/th>\n<th>Evidence in the computational experiment<\/th>\n<\/tr>\n<\/thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>A1<\/td>\n<td>Approach in the baseline case<\/td>\n<td>The simulated state\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>x<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nfirst reaches at least\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>3.6<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">3.6\\,\\mathrm K<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nby\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>t<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>90<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t=90\\,\\mathrm s<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>A2<\/td>\n<td>Control input in all cases<\/td>\n<td>Every recorded control input satisfies\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0<\/mn><mo>≤<\/mo><mi>u<\/mi><mo>≤<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0\\le u\\le1<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>A3<\/td>\n<td>Deviation after the disturbance begins<\/td>\n<td>In both disturbed cases,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|<\/mo><mn>4<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|<\/mo><mo>≤<\/mo><mn>0.10<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|4\\,\\mathrm K-x|\\le0.10\\,\\mathrm K<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nat every tested time from 420 to 720 s.<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>A4<\/td>\n<td>Documentation of the measurement outage<\/td>\n<td>The raw values are missing during the specified interval; the\nsubstitute value and associated status can be identified\nseparately.<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<p>A3 applies at the times investigated. A further test with a smaller\ntime step assesses the dependence on computational resolution. A4\nestablishes whether the data gap is correctly handled in the log. A3\ntests whether the room also maintains its temperature under these\nconditions.<\/p>\n<figure>\n<img src=\"../learning-courses-university-electrical-engineering-en/media/img/U_ELG_139_EN.svg\"\nalt=\"Timeline from zero to 720 seconds showing requirements A1 to A4, onset of the disturbance at 240 seconds and the measurement gap from 250 seconds.\" />\n<figcaption>Figure: The timeline assigns distinct times and intervals to\nrequirements A1–A4; disturbance onset and missing measurements are\nmarked, not whether requirements pass.<\/figcaption>\n<\/figure>\n<p>The coloured regions indicate the intended test times or time\nwindows, not the outcome of the test. A1 requires at least one\nqualifying sample by 90 seconds; A3, by contrast, requires the limit to\nbe satisfied at every tested time in the specified interval. For A4, the\nendpoint at 260 seconds is excluded.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S3\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Example: Deriving a precise criterion from an\nobservation<\/h2>\n<p>“Stable at the end” can mean different things in everyday language.\nSuppose a test shows two rows with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>400<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mn>3.86<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x(400\\,\\mathrm s)=3.86\\,\\mathrm K<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>720<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mn>4.01<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x(720\\,\\mathrm s)=4.01\\,\\mathrm K<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nThe final value is only\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.01<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0.01\\,\\mathrm K<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\naway from the reference. This is insufficient to decide A3, because A3\nrequires the <strong>maximum absolute error over an interval<\/strong>. A\nthird row with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>480<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mn>3.88<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x(480\\,\\mathrm s)=3.88\\,\\mathrm K<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nwould immediately disprove A3.<\/p>\n<p>We also distinguish between the purpose of a test and the applicable\nstandard of evidence. The log field for a substitute value can be tested\ndirectly. Evidence of actual temperature quality would require, among\nother things, a suitable thermometer, consideration of the spatial\ntemperature distribution and an independent experiment. A positive\nsimulation result is a statement about this configuration and these\ndisturbances.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S4\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Self-check<\/h2>\n<ol type=\"1\" class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">For an additional case, formulate a concrete limit on a single\novershoot of at most\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.20<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0.20\\,\\mathrm K<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nWhich value must you determine from the data?<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">The sample interval is half a second. How many raw values are\nmissing if the interval\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[<\/mo><mn>250<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mn>260<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">[250,260)<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nis sampled exactly?<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Why can a rejected data field in the log violate A4 even though the\ncurve satisfies A3?<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<h3 id=\"solutions\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Solutions<\/h3>\n<ol type=\"1\" class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">In this case,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">max<\/mi><mo>&#8289;<\/mo><\/mrow><mi>x<\/mi><mo>≤<\/mo><mn>4.20<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\max x\\le4.20\\,\\mathrm K<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nmust hold throughout the observation period specified in advance. During\nevaluation, the maximum simulated state value and its time are\nrecorded.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">There are\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>10<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>0.5<\/mn><mo>=<\/mo><mn>20<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">10/0.5=20<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nmissing raw values. The first missing value is at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>250<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">250\\,\\mathrm s<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nthe last at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>259.5<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">259.5\\,\\mathrm s<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">A4 tests the traceability of the measurement information. A\nplausible curve does not prove that the log makes the difference in\norigin between measured and substitute values visible.<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<h2 id=\"S5\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Project limitations and further study<\/h2>\n<p>The comparison demonstrates suitability for the specified scenarios\nwith a scalar state model. Statements about the operational safety of a\nheating system require other evidence and qualified professionals with\nappropriate responsibility. In <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering-core&amp;module=M8&amp;lesson=L2&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">M8-L2<\/a>,\nthe component models and their interfaces are developed.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S6\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Sources<\/h2>\n<ul class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a href=\"https://s.kit.edu/mhb-etit-bsc23\">KIT, B.Sc. Electrical\nEngineering and Information Technology, module handbook, winter semester\n2026/27<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a> · project work module M-ETIT-106629, § 13.56. · Last\naccessed: 2026-11-25<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://www.cit.tum.de/fileadmin/w00byx/cit/Studium/Studiengaenge/Bachelor_Elektrotechnik_Informationstechnik/Studienfuehrer_Bachelor_EI.pdf\">TUM,\nElectrical Engineering and Information Technology study guide<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a> · §§\n5.6–5.7 on engineering practice and the bachelor’s thesis. · Last\naccessed: 2026-11-25<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://www.nasa.gov/reference/appendix-d-requirements-verification-matrix/\">NASA\nSystems Engineering Handbook, Appendix D<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a> · unambiguous linking of\nrequirements and evidence · Last accessed: 2026-11-25<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/article>","university_electrical_engineering_core_en:M8-L2":"<article class=\"lesson-standard\"><h1 id=\"L2\">M8-L2 – Design of the Measurement Chain and Control Plant<\/h1>\n<p><strong>Course area:<\/strong> M8 – Bachelor: Engineering Practice and Bachelor’s Project<\/p>\n<p><strong>Level:<\/strong> Bachelor<\/p>\n<p><strong>Prerequisites:<\/strong> <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering-core&amp;module=M8&amp;lesson=L1&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">Project\nrequirements<\/a>, <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering-core&amp;module=M6&amp;lesson=L3&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">Step\nresponse<\/a> and <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering-core&amp;module=M6&amp;lesson=L5&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">Stability and\nintroduction to controllers<\/a>.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Learning objective:<\/strong> Formulate plant, measurement and\ncontroller models using consistent quantities. Calculate the most\nimportant expected values before simulation.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S1\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>From the problem statement to the interface<\/h2>\n<p>The plant supplies the temperature rise\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>x<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nin kelvin. The measurement chain converts\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>x<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\ninto a raw signal\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>m<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand estimates the calibrated measurement value\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>y<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nfrom it. The controller uses\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>y<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nto form the error\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>e<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>r<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mi>y<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">e=r-y<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nIt supplies the dimensionless control input\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>u<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">u<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nlimited to the interval\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">[0,1]<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nThe reference\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>r<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand disturbance\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>d<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nare modelled in kelvin.\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>d<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nis an equivalent input to the plant that shifts its equilibrium\nvalue.<\/p>\n<figure>\n<img src=\"../learning-courses-university-electrical-engineering-en/media/img/U_ELG_020_EN.svg\"\nalt=\"Block diagram of a feedback-controlled plant. The numerical temperature state is captured by the measurement chain and fed back to the controller.\" />\n<figcaption>Figure: The schematic temperature model joins reference\ncomparison, PI controller, plant and measurement chain through negative\nfeedback; a disturbance enters at the plant.<\/figcaption>\n<\/figure>\n<h2 id=\"S2\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Plant model and units<\/h2>\n<p>The state dynamics are<\/p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ<\/mi><mover><mi>x<\/mi><mo accent=\"true\">̇<\/mo><\/mover><mo>+<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><msub><mi>K<\/mi><mi>u<\/mi><\/msub><mi>u<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mi>d<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mspace width=\"2.0em\"><\/mspace><mi>τ<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>60<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mspace width=\"1.0em\"><\/mspace><msub><mi>K<\/mi><mi>u<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mn>10<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><mi>.<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\tau\\dot x+x=K_u u+d,\\qquad \\tau=60\\,\\mathrm s,\\quad K_u=10\\,\\mathrm{K}.<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/p>\n<p>Since\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>u<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">u<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nis dimensionless,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>K<\/mi><mi>u<\/mi><\/msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K_u<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\ncan be specified in kelvin.\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ<\/mi><mover><mi>x<\/mi><mo accent=\"true\">̇<\/mo><\/mover><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\tau\\dot x<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nhas units of kelvin. A constant control input\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mover><mi>u<\/mi><mo accent=\"true\">‾<\/mo><\/mover><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\bar u<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand a constant disturbance\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mover><mi>d<\/mi><mo accent=\"true\">‾<\/mo><\/mover><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\bar d<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nyield the steady-state value\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mover><mi>x<\/mi><mo accent=\"true\">‾<\/mo><\/mover><mo>=<\/mo><msub><mi>K<\/mi><mi>u<\/mi><\/msub><mover><mi>u<\/mi><mo accent=\"true\">‾<\/mo><\/mover><mo>+<\/mo><mover><mi>d<\/mi><mo accent=\"true\">‾<\/mo><\/mover><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\bar x=K_u\\bar u+\\bar d<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nFor\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>r<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>4<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r=4\\,\\mathrm K<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nthe disturbance-free equilibrium would require\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>u<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0.4<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">u=0.4<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nWith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>−<\/mi><mn>1<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d=-1\\,\\mathrm K<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nit requires\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>u<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0.5<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">u=0.5<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.<\/p>\n<p>The controller calculation uses the integrator state\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>z<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">z<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nin control-input units. The proportional gain is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K<\/mi><mi>p<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0.20<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><mrow><mi>−<\/mi><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><\/msup><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K_p=0.20\\,\\mathrm K^{-1}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand the integral gain is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K<\/mi><mi>i<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><msub><mi>K<\/mi><mi>p<\/mi><\/msub><mi>/<\/mi><mi>τ<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K_i=K_p/\\tau<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nIn the linear model,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mover><mi>z<\/mi><mo accent=\"true\">̇<\/mo><\/mover><mo>=<\/mo><msub><mi>K<\/mi><mi>i<\/mi><\/msub><mi>e<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\dot z=K_i e<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nThe unconstrained control input is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K<\/mi><mi>p<\/mi><\/msub><mi>e<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mi>z<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K_p e+z<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nWhen limiting the input, integration in the direction of a control-input\nlimit that has already been reached is suspended. When the unconstrained\ncontrol input falls back, the integrator can resume normal operation.\nThis conditional integration is the anti-windup rule used here.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S3\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Measurement model and calibration<\/h2>\n<p>For the raw signal in volts, we assume:<\/p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>m<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mi>g<\/mi><mi>x<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mi>n<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mspace width=\"2.0em\"><\/mspace><mi>b<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0.30<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V<\/mi><mo>,<\/mo><mspace width=\"1.0em\"><\/mspace><mi>g<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>1.02<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><\/mrow><mi>.<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m=b+g x+n,\\qquad\nb=0.30\\,\\mathrm V,\\quad\ng=1.02\\,\\mathrm{V/K}.<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/p>\n<p>The calibrated estimate is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>m<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mi>b<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mi>/<\/mi><mi>g<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y=(m-b)/g<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nFor the <strong>measurement chain<\/strong> case, the simulation uses a\nprescribed deviation\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0.05<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin<\/mi><mo>&#8289;<\/mo><\/mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>2<\/mn><mi>π<\/mi><mi>t<\/mi><mi>/<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>20<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n=0.05\\,\\mathrm V\\sin(2\\pi t/(20\\,\\mathrm s))<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nThe resulting measurement error has a peak value of\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.05<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V<\/mi><mi>/<\/mi><mi>g<\/mi><mo>≈<\/mo><mn>0.0490<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0.05\\,\\mathrm V/g\\approx0.0490\\,\\mathrm K<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nThe sinusoidal disturbance is used to reproduce the same deviation\nexactly in every run.<\/p>\n<p>During the ten-second measurement gap,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>y<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nremains at the last valid value. Integration of the state\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>x<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\ncontinues. Each substitute value receives a status flag. This behaviour\nmodels a limited test case. A longer gap would require a separate\nfault-handling requirement.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S4\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Example: Initial values and plausibility<\/h2>\n<p>Initially,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mi>z<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x(0)=z(0)=0<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nWithout measurement deviation, calibration gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y(0)=0<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nThe initial control input is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>u<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0.20<\/mn><mo>⋅<\/mo><mn>4<\/mn><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0.8<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">u(0)=0.20\\cdot4=0.8<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nWith\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d=0<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nthe state rate is<\/p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mover><mi>x<\/mi><mo accent=\"true\">̇<\/mo><\/mover><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>10<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><mo>⋅<\/mo><mn>0.8<\/mn><\/mrow><mrow><mn>60<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s<\/mi><\/mrow><\/mfrac><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0.1333<\/mn><mi>…<\/mi><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s<\/mi><\/mrow><mi>.<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\dot x(0)=\\frac{10\\,\\mathrm K\\cdot0.8}{60\\,\\mathrm s}\n=0.1333\\ldots\\,\\mathrm{K/s}.<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/p>\n<p>An explicit Euler step of one second therefore gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0.1333<\/mn><mi>…<\/mi><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x(1\\,\\mathrm s)=0.1333\\ldots\\,\\mathrm K<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nIt starts with the values at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>t<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t=0<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nIf the code updated\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>z<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">z<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nbefore this calculation and immediately used the newly calculated\ncontrol input, it would implement a different discrete method. The first\nhand-calculated value is therefore a useful test of the update\norder.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S5\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Self-check<\/h2>\n<ol type=\"1\" class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">A raw value is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>m<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>3.36<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m=3.36\\,\\mathrm V<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nDetermine\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>y<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nusing the specified calibration.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">What disturbance\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>d<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nis present at equilibrium when\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>u<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0.65<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">u=0.65<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>4<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x=4\\,\\mathrm K<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>?<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">At\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>e<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">e=1\\,\\mathrm K<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>z<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0.9<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">z=0.9<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nthe controller proposes\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>u<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>1.1<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">u=1.1<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nWhat does the limiter return, and how does the integrator behave?<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<h3 id=\"solutions\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Solutions<\/h3>\n<ol type=\"1\" class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>3.36<\/mn><mo>−<\/mo><mn>0.30<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mi>/<\/mi><mn>1.02<\/mn><mo>=<\/mo><mn>3<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(3.36-0.30)/1.02=3\\,\\mathrm K<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>d<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><msub><mi>K<\/mi><mi>u<\/mi><\/msub><mi>u<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>4<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mn>6.5<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>−<\/mi><mn>2.5<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d=x-K_u u=4\\,\\mathrm K-6.5\\,\\mathrm K=-2.5\\,\\mathrm K<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">The valid control input is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>u<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">u=1<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nSince\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>e<\/mi><mo>&gt;<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">e&gt;0<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nwould further increase the unconstrained control input,\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>z<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">z<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nremains unchanged during this step.<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<h2 id=\"S6\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Limitations and further study<\/h2>\n<p>Heat loss, room size and heating power are represented here by the\nsteady-state gain\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>K<\/mi><mi>u<\/mi><\/msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">K_u<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand by\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>τ<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\tau<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nThe measurement chain uses known calibration values. The uncertainty of\nthese parameters would need to be determined in a real measurement\nproject. <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering-core&amp;module=M8&amp;lesson=L3&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">M8-L3<\/a>\ncombines the models into a reproducible computational experiment.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S7\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Sources<\/h2>\n<ul class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://fbswiki.org/wiki/index.php/Feedback_Systems%3A_An_Introduction_for_Scientists_and_Engineers\">Åström/Murray\n– Feedback Systems, Second Edition<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a> · Chapter index 3, 5, 6, 9 and\n11: modeling, dynamics, linear systems, transfer functions and PID;\nlinked chapters not re-reviewed. · Last accessed: 2026-11-25<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a href=\"https://www.bipm.org/en/doi/10.59161/jcgm100-2008e\">JCGM\n100:2008, Guide to the Expression of Uncertainty in Measurement<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a> ·\nmeasurement model, input quantities and uncertainty · Last accessed:\n2026-11-25<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/article>","university_electrical_engineering_core_en:M8-L3":"<article class=\"lesson-standard\"><h1 id=\"L3\">M8-L3 – Simulation, Reference Values and Measurement Data<\/h1>\n<p><strong>Course area:<\/strong> M8 – Bachelor: Engineering Practice and Bachelor’s Project<\/p>\n<p><strong>Level:<\/strong> Bachelor<\/p>\n<p><strong>Prerequisites:<\/strong> <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering-core&amp;module=M8&amp;lesson=L1&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">Project\nrequirements<\/a>, <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering-core&amp;module=M8&amp;lesson=L2&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">Plant and\nmeasurement model<\/a> and <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering-core&amp;module=M2&amp;lesson=L7&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">Computational\nexperiments<\/a>.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Learning objective:<\/strong> Produce a reproducible\nsimulation run with documented inputs, raw values, state variables and\ntest metrics calculated from them.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S1\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Data flow and timeline<\/h2>\n<p>The model consistently uses seconds, kelvin for temperature\ndifferences and volts for the raw sensor value. At each time, the\ncurrent state\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>x<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_k<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nis measured first, the control input\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>u<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">u_k<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nis then calculated, and integration subsequently uses the values at that\ntime. For the Euler method with step size\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>h<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,<\/p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x<\/mi><mrow><mi>k<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><msub><mi>x<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><mo>+<\/mo><mfrac><mi>h<\/mi><mi>τ<\/mi><\/mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><msub><mi>K<\/mi><mi>u<\/mi><\/msub><msub><mi>u<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><mo>+<\/mo><msub><mi>d<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><mo>−<\/mo><msub><mi>x<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><mi>.<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_{k+1}=x_k+\\frac{h}{\\tau}\\left(K_u u_k+d_k-x_k\\right).<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/p>\n<p>The log contains both the simulated state\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>x<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_k<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand the measurement estimate\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>y<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y_k<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nThe simulated state serves here as the reference for the test metrics.\nIn a real installation, the controller generally knows this state only\nthrough measurements or an estimate. During the measurement gap, the\nfield for\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>m<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">m_k<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nis empty. The substitute value used remains visible in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>y<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y_k<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S2\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Reproducible computational experiment<\/h2>\n<p>The program requires the Python standard library. With a step size of\none second, it calculates 721 rows per case, including the time 720 s.\nThe control input specified there is recorded. For the reported time\ninterval, only inputs before that final time contribute to the evolution\nof the state. When saving the data, rows are distinguished by the name\nof each test case.<\/p>\n<div class=\"sourceCode\" id=\"cb1\"><pre\nclass=\"sourceCode python\"><code class=\"sourceCode python\"><span id=\"cb1-1\"><a href=\"#cb1-1\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"im\">import<\/span> csv<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-2\"><a href=\"#cb1-2\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"im\">import<\/span> math<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-3\"><a href=\"#cb1-3\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-4\"><a href=\"#cb1-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>TAU, GAIN, REF <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> <span class=\"fl\">60.0<\/span>, <span class=\"fl\">10.0<\/span>, <span class=\"fl\">4.0<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-5\"><a href=\"#cb1-5\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>KP, KI <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> <span class=\"fl\">0.2<\/span>, <span class=\"fl\">0.2<\/span> <span class=\"op\">/<\/span> TAU<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-6\"><a href=\"#cb1-6\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>OFFSET, SCALE <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> <span class=\"fl\">0.30<\/span>, <span class=\"fl\">1.02<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-7\"><a href=\"#cb1-7\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>CASES <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> (<span class=\"st\">&quot;basis&quot;<\/span>, <span class=\"st\">&quot;stoerung&quot;<\/span>, <span class=\"st\">&quot;messkette&quot;<\/span>)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-8\"><a href=\"#cb1-8\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-9\"><a href=\"#cb1-9\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"kw\">def<\/span> simulate(case, dt<span class=\"op\">=<\/span><span class=\"fl\">1.0<\/span>):<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-10\"><a href=\"#cb1-10\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">if<\/span> case <span class=\"kw\">not<\/span> <span class=\"kw\">in<\/span> CASES <span class=\"kw\">or<\/span> dt <span class=\"kw\">not<\/span> <span class=\"kw\">in<\/span> (<span class=\"fl\">1.0<\/span>, <span class=\"fl\">0.5<\/span>):<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-11\"><a href=\"#cb1-11\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        <span class=\"cf\">raise<\/span> <span class=\"pp\">ValueError<\/span>(<span class=\"st\">&quot;Unbekannter Fall oder Zeitschritt&quot;<\/span>)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-12\"><a href=\"#cb1-12\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    x, z, y <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> <span class=\"fl\">0.0<\/span>, <span class=\"fl\">0.0<\/span>, <span class=\"fl\">0.0<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-13\"><a href=\"#cb1-13\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    samples <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> []<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-14\"><a href=\"#cb1-14\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">for<\/span> k <span class=\"kw\">in<\/span> <span class=\"bu\">range<\/span>(<span class=\"bu\">int<\/span>(<span class=\"dv\">720<\/span> <span class=\"op\">/<\/span> dt) <span class=\"op\">+<\/span> <span class=\"dv\">1<\/span>):<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-15\"><a href=\"#cb1-15\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        t <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> k <span class=\"op\">*<\/span> dt<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-16\"><a href=\"#cb1-16\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        missing <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> case <span class=\"op\">==<\/span> <span class=\"st\">&quot;messkette&quot;<\/span> <span class=\"kw\">and<\/span> <span class=\"dv\">250<\/span> <span class=\"op\">&lt;=<\/span> t <span class=\"op\">&lt;<\/span> <span class=\"dv\">260<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-17\"><a href=\"#cb1-17\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        n <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> <span class=\"fl\">0.05<\/span> <span class=\"op\">*<\/span> math.sin(<span class=\"dv\">2<\/span> <span class=\"op\">*<\/span> math.pi <span class=\"op\">*<\/span> t <span class=\"op\">/<\/span> <span class=\"dv\">20<\/span>) <span class=\"cf\">if<\/span> case <span class=\"op\">==<\/span> <span class=\"st\">&quot;messkette&quot;<\/span> <span class=\"cf\">else<\/span> <span class=\"fl\">0.0<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-18\"><a href=\"#cb1-18\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        raw <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> <span class=\"va\">None<\/span> <span class=\"cf\">if<\/span> missing <span class=\"cf\">else<\/span> OFFSET <span class=\"op\">+<\/span> SCALE <span class=\"op\">*<\/span> x <span class=\"op\">+<\/span> n<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-19\"><a href=\"#cb1-19\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        <span class=\"cf\">if<\/span> raw <span class=\"kw\">is<\/span> <span class=\"kw\">not<\/span> <span class=\"va\">None<\/span>:<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-20\"><a href=\"#cb1-20\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>            y <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> (raw <span class=\"op\">-<\/span> OFFSET) <span class=\"op\">/<\/span> SCALE<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-21\"><a href=\"#cb1-21\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        d <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> <span class=\"op\">-<\/span><span class=\"fl\">1.0<\/span> <span class=\"cf\">if<\/span> case <span class=\"op\">!=<\/span> <span class=\"st\">&quot;basis&quot;<\/span> <span class=\"kw\">and<\/span> t <span class=\"op\">&gt;=<\/span> <span class=\"dv\">240<\/span> <span class=\"cf\">else<\/span> <span class=\"fl\">0.0<\/span><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-22\"><a href=\"#cb1-22\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-23\"><a href=\"#cb1-23\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        e <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> REF <span class=\"op\">-<\/span> y<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-24\"><a href=\"#cb1-24\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        proposal <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> KP <span class=\"op\">*<\/span> e <span class=\"op\">+<\/span> z<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-25\"><a href=\"#cb1-25\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        u <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> <span class=\"bu\">min<\/span>(<span class=\"fl\">1.0<\/span>, <span class=\"bu\">max<\/span>(<span class=\"fl\">0.0<\/span>, proposal))<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-26\"><a href=\"#cb1-26\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        deeper <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> (proposal <span class=\"op\">&gt;=<\/span> <span class=\"dv\">1<\/span> <span class=\"kw\">and<\/span> e <span class=\"op\">&gt;<\/span> <span class=\"dv\">0<\/span>) <span class=\"kw\">or<\/span> (proposal <span class=\"op\">&lt;=<\/span> <span class=\"dv\">0<\/span> <span class=\"kw\">and<\/span> e <span class=\"op\">&lt;<\/span> <span class=\"dv\">0<\/span>)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-27\"><a href=\"#cb1-27\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        samples.append((t, x, raw, y, u, d, <span class=\"bu\">int<\/span>(missing)))<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-28\"><a href=\"#cb1-28\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        <span class=\"cf\">if<\/span> <span class=\"kw\">not<\/span> deeper:<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-29\"><a href=\"#cb1-29\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>            z <span class=\"op\">+=<\/span> dt <span class=\"op\">*<\/span> KI <span class=\"op\">*<\/span> e<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-30\"><a href=\"#cb1-30\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        x <span class=\"op\">+=<\/span> dt <span class=\"op\">*<\/span> (GAIN <span class=\"op\">*<\/span> u <span class=\"op\">+<\/span> d <span class=\"op\">-<\/span> x) <span class=\"op\">/<\/span> TAU<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-31\"><a href=\"#cb1-31\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">return<\/span> samples<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-32\"><a href=\"#cb1-32\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-33\"><a href=\"#cb1-33\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"kw\">def<\/span> metrics(rows):<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-34\"><a href=\"#cb1-34\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    arrival <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> <span class=\"bu\">next<\/span>(t <span class=\"cf\">for<\/span> t, x, <span class=\"op\">*<\/span>_ <span class=\"kw\">in<\/span> rows <span class=\"cf\">if<\/span> x <span class=\"op\">&gt;=<\/span> <span class=\"fl\">3.6<\/span>)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-35\"><a href=\"#cb1-35\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    max_after <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> <span class=\"bu\">max<\/span>(<span class=\"bu\">abs<\/span>(x <span class=\"op\">-<\/span> REF) <span class=\"cf\">for<\/span> t, x, <span class=\"op\">*<\/span>_ <span class=\"kw\">in<\/span> rows <span class=\"cf\">if<\/span> t <span class=\"op\">&gt;=<\/span> <span class=\"dv\">420<\/span>)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-36\"><a href=\"#cb1-36\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">return<\/span> arrival, max_after, <span class=\"bu\">sum<\/span>(row[<span class=\"op\">-<\/span><span class=\"dv\">1<\/span>] <span class=\"cf\">for<\/span> row <span class=\"kw\">in<\/span> rows)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-37\"><a href=\"#cb1-37\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-38\"><a href=\"#cb1-38\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a><span class=\"cf\">with<\/span> <span class=\"bu\">open<\/span>(<span class=\"st\">&quot;temperaturprojekt.csv&quot;<\/span>, <span class=\"st\">&quot;w&quot;<\/span>, encoding<span class=\"op\">=<\/span><span class=\"st\">&quot;utf-8&quot;<\/span>, newline<span class=\"op\">=<\/span><span class=\"st\">&quot;&quot;<\/span>) <span class=\"im\">as<\/span> <span class=\"bu\">file<\/span>:<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-39\"><a href=\"#cb1-39\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    writer <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> csv.writer(<span class=\"bu\">file<\/span>)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-40\"><a href=\"#cb1-40\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    writer.writerow((<span class=\"st\">&quot;fall&quot;<\/span>, <span class=\"st\">&quot;t_s&quot;<\/span>, <span class=\"st\">&quot;x_K&quot;<\/span>, <span class=\"st\">&quot;roh_V&quot;<\/span>, <span class=\"st\">&quot;y_K&quot;<\/span>, <span class=\"st\">&quot;u&quot;<\/span>, <span class=\"st\">&quot;d_K&quot;<\/span>, <span class=\"st\">&quot;luecke&quot;<\/span>))<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-41\"><a href=\"#cb1-41\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>    <span class=\"cf\">for<\/span> case <span class=\"kw\">in<\/span> CASES:<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-42\"><a href=\"#cb1-42\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        rows <span class=\"op\">=<\/span> simulate(case)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-43\"><a href=\"#cb1-43\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        <span class=\"cf\">assert<\/span> <span class=\"bu\">all<\/span>(<span class=\"dv\">0<\/span> <span class=\"op\">&lt;=<\/span> row[<span class=\"dv\">4<\/span>] <span class=\"op\">&lt;=<\/span> <span class=\"dv\">1<\/span> <span class=\"cf\">for<\/span> row <span class=\"kw\">in<\/span> rows)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-44\"><a href=\"#cb1-44\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        writer.writerows((case, <span class=\"op\">*<\/span>row) <span class=\"cf\">for<\/span> row <span class=\"kw\">in<\/span> rows)<\/span>\n<span id=\"cb1-45\"><a href=\"#cb1-45\" aria-hidden=\"true\" tabindex=\"-1\"><\/a>        <span class=\"bu\">print<\/span>(case, metrics(rows))<\/span><\/code><\/pre><\/div>\n<p>The file <em>temperaturprojekt.csv<\/em> is created in the working\ndirectory. The three columns for the raw value, the calibrated value\nused and the gap status help test the data handling separately. The\noriginal code retains its German CSV labels and case names\n(<code>basis<\/code> = baseline, <code>stoerung<\/code> = disturbance,\n<code>messkette<\/code> = measurement chain; <code>fall<\/code> = case,\n<code>roh_V<\/code> = raw value in volts, <code>luecke<\/code> = gap). To\ncompare a different step size, run the same function with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0.5<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h=0.5\\,\\mathrm s<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand record the results separately.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S3\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Expected test values<\/h2>\n<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col class=\"lc-col-width-20\">\n<col class=\"lc-col-width-26\">\n<col class=\"lc-col-width-26\">\n<col class=\"lc-col-width-26\">\n<\/colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Case at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h=1\\,\\mathrm s<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/th>\n<th class=\"text-right\">First sample with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><mo>≥<\/mo><mn>3.6<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x\\ge3.6\\,\\mathrm K<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/th>\n<th class=\"text-right\">Maximum absolute reference error from 420\ns<\/th>\n<th class=\"text-right\">Missing raw values<\/th>\n<\/tr>\n<\/thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Baseline<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">68 s<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">approximately\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.000003<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0.000003\\,\\mathrm K<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">0<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Disturbance<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">68 s<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\"><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.046309<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0.046309\\,\\mathrm K<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">0<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Measurement chain<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">69 s<\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\"><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.045113<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0.045113\\,\\mathrm K<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/td>\n<td class=\"text-right\">10<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<p>In the <strong>measurement chain<\/strong> case, the estimate at the\nstart of the outage at 250 s is approximately\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>3.886769<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">3.886769\\,\\mathrm K<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nIt stays constant up to and including 259 s. The actual simulated state\nfalls during that period from approximately\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>3.861068<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">3.861068\\,\\mathrm K<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nto\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>3.776376<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">3.776376\\,\\mathrm K<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nThe difference illustrates why a held signal must be flagged in the\nfile.<\/p>\n<figure>\n<img src=\"../learning-courses-university-electrical-engineering-en/media/img/U_ELG_140_EN.svg\"\nalt=\"Time histories of the simulated state and the measurement estimate used from 240 to 275 seconds; ten seconds without raw values are shaded.\" />\n<figcaption>Figure: During the ten-second gap in raw measurements, the\nlast available reading is held as the estimate; the simulated state\ncontinues evolving separately.<\/figcaption>\n<\/figure>\n<p>The points come from the program in this lesson. The lines connect\nthe discrete samples as a visual guide; they do not represent additional\nmeasurement resolution. During the shaded period, no raw values are\navailable. The green curve does not describe new sensor measurements,\nbut the held substitute value.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S4\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Self-check<\/h2>\n<ol type=\"1\" class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">How many data rows are generated for three cases and a time step of\none second? Count the header row separately.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">In the measurement chain case, the true state at 250 s is\napproximately\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>3.861068<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">3.861068\\,\\mathrm K<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nand the substitute value is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>3.886769<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">3.886769\\,\\mathrm K<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nHow large is the difference\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y-x<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>?<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Why can the climate-control reference in a log’s raw-value column\nneither be directly compared with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>4<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">4\\,\\mathrm K<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nnor be read from an empty cell?<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<h3 id=\"solutions\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Solutions<\/h3>\n<ol type=\"1\" class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Each case has 721 rows, giving a total of 2163 data rows plus one\nheader row.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">The difference is approximately\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>+<\/mi><mn>0.025701<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">+0.025701\\,\\mathrm K<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nIn this row, the value that continues to be used overestimates the\nsimulated state.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">The raw value is a voltage and requires calibration. An empty cell\nsignifies a measurement gap. Separate columns are provided for the\nsubstitute value used and the status.<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<h2 id=\"S5\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Limitations and further study<\/h2>\n<p>The comparison is deterministic. Other sensor deviations, longer\noutages and changed model parameters are separate test cases. A\nreproducible file initially demonstrates that the same calculation can\nbe repeated with the same inputs. <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering-core&amp;module=M8&amp;lesson=L4&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">M8-L4<\/a>\nadditionally tests whether the model satisfies the selected references\nand assumptions.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S6\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Sources<\/h2>\n<ul class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://www.nationalacademies.org/read/25303/chapter/3\">National\nAcademies, Reproducibility and Replicability in Science<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a> · summary on\ncomputational reproducibility with the same inputs, computational steps\nand conditions · Last accessed: 2026-11-25<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://fbswiki.org/wiki/index.php/Feedback_Systems%3A_An_Introduction_for_Scientists_and_Engineers\">Åström/Murray\n– Feedback Systems, Second Edition<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a> · Chapter index 3, 5, 6, 9 and\n11: modeling, dynamics, linear systems, transfer functions and PID;\nlinked chapters not re-reviewed. · Last accessed: 2026-11-25<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/article>","university_electrical_engineering_core_en:M8-L4":"<article class=\"lesson-standard\"><h1 id=\"L4\">M8-L4 – Model Validation and Troubleshooting<\/h1>\n<p><strong>Course area:<\/strong> M8 – Bachelor: Engineering Practice and Bachelor’s Project<\/p>\n<p><strong>Level:<\/strong> Bachelor<\/p>\n<p><strong>Prerequisites:<\/strong> <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering-core&amp;module=M8&amp;lesson=L3&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">Computational\nexperiment and data sets<\/a>, <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering-core&amp;module=M2&amp;lesson=L3&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">Linear\ndifferential equations<\/a> and <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering-core&amp;module=M6&amp;lesson=L5&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">Stability<\/a>.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Learning objective:<\/strong> Distinguish computational\nerrors, model discrepancies and measurement problems using different\ntypes of comparative data.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S1\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Different questions require different evidence<\/h2>\n<p>The implementation is consistent if the code solves the specified\nequations correctly. Model suitability is a separate question. A\ncomputational result may match an incomplete model precisely. We\ntherefore examine an analytically solvable reference case, sensitivity\nto the numerical time step and the deviation from a separately defined\ntest plant.<\/p>\n<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col class=\"lc-col-width-50\">\n<col class=\"lc-col-width-50\">\n<\/colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Question<\/th>\n<th>Suitable comparison<\/th>\n<\/tr>\n<\/thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Is the state update correct?<\/td>\n<td>Hand calculation of the first time step and analytical baseline\ncase.<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Do the verification results depend strongly on the time step?<\/td>\n<td>Repeat with 1 s and 0.5 s.<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Does the model explain a test plant with different parameters?<\/td>\n<td>Compare the model trajectory with independent reference values and\ndocument the residual.<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Can missing raw data be identified?<\/td>\n<td>Directly test the time boundaries, empty field and status flag.<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<h2 id=\"S2\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Analytical check and time-step comparison<\/h2>\n<p>In the baseline case with ideal measurement, the control input\nremains within its limits. With the plant\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>10<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>60<\/mn><mi>s<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">10/(60s+1)<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand PI controller\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.20<\/mn><mo>+<\/mo><mn>0.20<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>60<\/mn><mi>s<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0.20+0.20/(60s)<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nthe closed-loop reference-to-output transfer function is\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>30<\/mn><mi>s<\/mi><mo>+<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1/(30s+1)<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nThe exact continuous solution for the reference step is<\/p>\n<p><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mi>t<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mn>4<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo>−<\/mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e<\/mi><mrow><mi>−<\/mi><mi>t<\/mi><mi>/<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>30<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><\/msup><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><mi>.<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x(t)=4\\,\\mathrm K\\left(1-\\mathrm e^{-t/(30\\,\\mathrm s)}\\right).<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/p>\n<p>At\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>t<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>30<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t=30\\,\\mathrm s<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nit gives approximately\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>2.5285<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">2.5285\\,\\mathrm K<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nThe Euler run with a one-second step gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>2.5534<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">2.5534\\,\\mathrm K<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nat that time. The difference of approximately\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.0249<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0.0249\\,\\mathrm K<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\ncan be attributed to discretisation. It occurs in the deterministic\nbaseline case before any measurement gap. The first sample reaching\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>3.6<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">3.6\\,\\mathrm K<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\noccurs at 68 s in the coarser run and at 69 s in the run with half the\nstep size. The continuous equation reaches the threshold at\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>30<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ln<\/mi><mo>&#8289;<\/mo><\/mrow><mn>10<\/mn><mo>≈<\/mo><mn>69.08<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">30\\,\\mathrm s\\ln 10\\approx69.08\\,\\mathrm s<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.<\/p>\n<p>In the disturbed case, the largest error after 420 s rises from\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.046309<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0.046309\\,\\mathrm K<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nto\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.046812<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0.046812\\,\\mathrm K<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nwhen the time step is halved. Both results are below\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.10<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0.10\\,\\mathrm K<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nIn the measurement chain case, 10 and 20 rows respectively are flagged\nwithin the gap. Its duration remains unchanged.<\/p>\n<figure>\n<img src=\"../learning-courses-university-electrical-engineering-en/media/img/U_ELG_021_EN.svg\"\nalt=\"Temperature rise curve in the baseline case. The analytical reference and the Euler samples are compared using the value at 30 seconds.\" />\n<figcaption>Figure: Euler samples computed at 1 s intervals track the\nanalytical temperature curve, with a small discretisation error at 30\ns.<\/figcaption>\n<\/figure>\n<h2 id=\"S3\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Cross-check: the test plant responds more slowly<\/h2>\n<p>In an additional synthetic experiment, a constant control input\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>u<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0.4<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">u=0.4<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nreplaces the PI controller. The test plant has\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>72<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\tau=72\\,\\mathrm s<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nIt gives approximately\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>2.262<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">2.262\\,\\mathrm K<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nat 60 s. The original model with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>60<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\tau=60\\,\\mathrm s<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\ngives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>2.528<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">2.528\\,\\mathrm K<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nThe residual\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><mo>−<\/mo><msub><mi>x<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l<\/mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l<\/mi><\/mrow><\/msub><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_\\mathrm{Test}-x_\\mathrm{Modell}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nis therefore approximately\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>−<\/mi><mn>0.267<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">-0.267\\,\\mathrm K<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\n(the subscripts denote the test plant and the model).<\/p>\n<p>The sign is consistent with the slower test plant. If deviations at\nseveral times follow a similar pattern, the time constant may offer an\nexplanation. A single value also allows for a different steady-state\ngain, measurement calibration errors or an incorrectly aligned time\naxis. Several samples, the final value and a second run should therefore\nbe examined. The synthetic counterexample tests the troubleshooting\nprocedure. Demonstrating validity for an actual room requires real\ncomparative data.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S4\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Self-assessment<\/h2>\n<ol type=\"1\" class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">For\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x(0)=0<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nand\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x<\/mi><mi>∞<\/mi><\/msub><mo>=<\/mo><mn>4<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_\\infty=4\\,\\mathrm K<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nan open-loop test gives\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>2.5285<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x=2.5285\\,\\mathrm K<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nat 60 s. Estimate the time constant using the first-order model.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">In a log with\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h=1\\,\\mathrm s<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\nraw values are missing from 250 s through 260 s inclusive. How does this\ndiffer from the requirement?<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Why is a comparison of two Euler step sizes alone weaker than a\ncomparison with the analytical solution?<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<h3 id=\"solutions\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Solutions<\/h3>\n<ol type=\"1\" class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">The normalised deviation from the final value is approximately\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1<\/mn><mo>−<\/mo><mn>2.5285<\/mn><mi>/<\/mi><mn>4<\/mn><mo>=<\/mo><mn>0.3679<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1-2.5285/4=0.3679<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nThus\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mi>−<\/mi><mn>60<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s<\/mi><mi>/<\/mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ln<\/mi><mo>&#8289;<\/mo><\/mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(<\/mo><mn>0.3679<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)<\/mo><mo>≈<\/mo><mn>60<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\tau=-60\\,\\mathrm s/\\ln(0.3679)\\approx60\\,\\mathrm s<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">The upper boundary of the interval is exclusive. At 260 s there must\nalready be a valid raw value. Eleven flagged rows would indicate a\nboundary error in the implementation.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Both Euler runs may share an implementation error. The independently\nderived solution provides a reference for the model calculation in the\nsimplified case.<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<h2 id=\"S5\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Limitations and further learning<\/h2>\n<p>The thresholds are checked at discrete samples. Rare deviations\nbetween two samples would require a finer simulation or an analytical\nbound. <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering-core&amp;module=M8&amp;lesson=L5&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">M8-L5<\/a>\nincorporates the findings into the report and verification matrix.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S6\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Sources<\/h2>\n<ul class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://fbswiki.org/wiki/index.php/Feedback_Systems%3A_An_Introduction_for_Scientists_and_Engineers\">Åström/Murray\n– Feedback Systems, Second Edition<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a> · Chapter index 3, 5, 6, 9 and\n11: modeling, dynamics, linear systems, transfer functions and PID;\nlinked chapters not re-reviewed. · Last accessed: 2026-11-25<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://www.nasa.gov/reference/appendix-d-requirements-verification-matrix/\">NASA\nSystems Engineering Handbook, Appendix D<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a> · traceability to evidence\nand verification methods · Last accessed: 2026-11-25<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/article>","university_electrical_engineering_core_en:M8-L5":"<article class=\"lesson-standard\"><h1 id=\"L5\">M8-L5 – Technical Reporting and Reproducibility<\/h1>\n<p><strong>Course area:<\/strong> M8 – Bachelor: Engineering Practice and Bachelor’s Project<\/p>\n<p><strong>Level:<\/strong> Bachelor<\/p>\n<p><strong>Prerequisites:<\/strong> <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering-core&amp;module=M8&amp;lesson=L1&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">Requirements\nmatrix<\/a>, <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering-core&amp;module=M8&amp;lesson=L3&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">Data log<\/a>\nand <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering-core&amp;module=M8&amp;lesson=L4&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">Reference\ntests<\/a>.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Learning objective:<\/strong> Write a verifiable technical\nproject report that clearly identifies decisions, results, uncertainties\nand limitations.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S1\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Report and verification evidence<\/h2>\n<p>Begin the report with the project question and the most important\nresult. Describe the temperature difference as the target quantity, the\ncases tested, the model assumptions and the underlying data. Details of\nthe simulation loop belong in the methods section or an appendix. A\nsingle figure in the main text is sufficient if it supports the\nverification decision and identifies the time axis, units, reference\nvalue and onset of the disturbance. Each row of the verification matrix\nshows which test supports the corresponding statement.<\/p>\n<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col class=\"lc-col-third\">\n<col class=\"lc-col-third\">\n<col class=\"lc-col-third\">\n<\/colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>ID<\/th>\n<th>Finding for\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h<\/mi><mo>=<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h=1\\,\\mathrm s<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math><\/th>\n<th>Evidence<\/th>\n<\/tr>\n<\/thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>A1<\/td>\n<td>Met. The first sample reaching\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>3.6<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">3.6\\,\\mathrm K<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nin the baseline case occurs at 68 s.<\/td>\n<td>Column\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>x<\/mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nof the baseline data.<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>A2<\/td>\n<td>Met. All logged control inputs lie in\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">[<\/mo><mn>0<\/mn><mo>,<\/mo><mn>1<\/mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">]<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">[0,1]<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.<\/td>\n<td>Range check of the control input column for all three test\ncases.<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>A3<\/td>\n<td>Met. Largest verified reference tracking error:\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.046309<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0.046309\\,\\mathrm K<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nin the disturbed case and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.045113<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0.045113\\,\\mathrm K<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nin the measurement chain case.<\/td>\n<td>Maximum absolute error across the rows from 420 s onwards.<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>A4<\/td>\n<td>Met. Exactly ten raw values are missing. The status and held\nestimate are visible.<\/td>\n<td>Time comparison for the rows from 250 to 259 s.<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<p>The statement “A2 met” is narrower than a statement about the\nfeasibility of the heating power. A2 checks a dimensionless model input\nwhose limit is part of the program. Whether an implemented system can\nsafely and accurately realise a corresponding control input requires\nadditional requirements and evidence.<\/p>\n<figure>\n<img src=\"../learning-courses-university-electrical-engineering-en/media/img/U_ELG_141_EN.svg\"\nalt=\"Absolute reference tracking error of the two disturbed cases during the verification interval from 420 to 720 seconds, with a requirement limit of 0.10 kelvin.\" />\n<figcaption>Figure: Across the modelled test interval 420–720 s, maximum\nabsolute setpoint errors in both disturbance cases remain below 0.10 K;\nthis is not experimental evidence.<\/figcaption>\n<\/figure>\n<p>The plotted interval contains all 301 verification samples for each\ncase. The largest absolute error is determined from these values, not\nfrom the final value. The figure thus provides direct evidence for A3 in\nthe numerical model; other requirements and the actual system require\nseparate evidence.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S2\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Report numerical values with appropriate precision<\/h2>\n<p>The verification matrix allows the exact value recorded by the\nprogram to be located. In the results summary, “approximately\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.05<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0.05\\,\\mathrm K<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nmaximum error after 420 s” is sufficient. In the disturbed case, halving\nthe time step changes this verification value by approximately\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.0005<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0.0005\\,\\mathrm K<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>.\nThis describes numerical sensitivity in this comparison. It is not an\nestablished measurement uncertainty for an actual device.<\/p>\n<p>Separate the assumptions behind uncertainties according to their\norigin. Time resolution comes from the computational method. Sensor\ngain, offset and possible drift originate in the measurement chain. An\nunmodelled spatial temperature distribution concerns the choice of\nmodel. Use a quantitative uncertainty budget only for quantities with\ntraceable input data.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S3\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Reproduction instructions and final review<\/h2>\n<p>Another person needs the program text from the lesson, the Python\nversion used, the inputs for all three cases and a description of the\ngenerated file. They should be able to reproduce the same threshold\ndecision. Brief reproduction instructions specify the directory where\nthe run generates its CSV and which columns and time intervals to\nevaluate. When comparing two versions later, it should be clear whether\nthe model, data processing or only the presentation was changed.<\/p>\n<p>A concise final report may have the following structure:<\/p>\n<ol type=\"1\" class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Question, scope, verification criteria.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Plant, measurement and controller models with units.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Test cases, program version and data provenance.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Results, verification matrix and comparison runs.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">5.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Limitations, open questions and reproduction instructions.<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>Good scientific practice begins when experiments are recorded. Retain\na run that failed a requirement if it provides technical insight.\nExplain corrections to the model or calculation and their effects on the\nconclusion.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S4\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Self-assessment<\/h2>\n<ol type=\"1\" class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Write a defensible one-sentence summary of A3. It should include the\noutcome, scenarios and time interval.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">A report contains two rounded figures for A3. How can you verify the\nclaim without running the program again?<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Propose an additional test for a substantially longer measurement\ngap. What information should be specified in the requirement before the\ntest is performed?<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<h3 id=\"solutions\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Solutions<\/h3>\n<ol type=\"1\" class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">“In the two simulated cases with a cooling disturbance, the absolute\nreference tracking error was below\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.10<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0.10\\,\\mathrm K<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nat all verified time points from 420 to 720 s.”<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Use the saved CSV, filter by the two test cases and\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>420<\/mn><mo>≤<\/mo><mi>t<\/mi><mo>≤<\/mo><mn>720<\/mn><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">420\\le t\\le720<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>,\ncalculate\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|<\/mo><mn>4<\/mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"><\/mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K<\/mi><mo>−<\/mo><mi>x<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">|4\\,\\mathrm K-x|<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>\nfor each row and compare the respective maxima with the threshold.<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3.<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\">Specify the start and duration of the gap, substitute-value\nstrategy, observation interval and permissible deviation. Specify\nseparately when the failure status must be visible. The assessment\ndepends on the purpose of the test.<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<h2 id=\"S5\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Completion and further learning<\/h2>\n<p>This project enables the reader to trace the engineering process from\nrequirements and models through data to the report. The <a\nhref=\"index.html?course=university_electrical-engineering-core&amp;page=study-path&amp;syslang=en&amp;doclang=en&amp;theme=light\">study\npathway<\/a> identifies the subsequent elective modules to which the same\nverification structure can be applied.<\/p>\n<h2 id=\"S6\"><span class=\"section-number\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span>Sources<\/h2>\n<ul class=\"lc-content-list\" role=\"list\">\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a href=\"https://s.kit.edu/mhb-etit-bsc23\">KIT, B.Sc. Electrical\nEngineering and Information Technology, module handbook, winter semester\n2026/27<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a> · § 13.56, project work following good scientific practice.\n· Last accessed: 2026-11-25<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a\nhref=\"https://www.nationalacademies.org/read/25303/chapter/3\">National\nAcademies, Reproducibility and Replicability in Science<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a> · summary on\nreproducible computational studies · Last accessed: 2026-11-25<\/div><\/li>\n<li role=\"listitem\"><span class=\"lc-item-marker\" aria-hidden=\"true\">•<\/span><div class=\"lc-item-content\"><a href=\"https://www.bipm.org/en/doi/10.59161/jcgm100-2008e\">JCGM\n100:2008, Guide to the Expression of Uncertainty in Measurement<span class=\"lc-external-arrow\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&#8239;↗<\/span><span class=\"sr-only lc-external-hint\"> (external link)<\/span><\/a> ·\nscope and documentation of measurement uncertainty · Last accessed:\n2026-11-25<\/div><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/article>"};
